{"title": "Monado: HP Reverb G2", "parts": {"header": "<div class=\"sd ex-sd\"><div class=sd-grid><div class=sd-head><span class=\"sd-maker none\">Collabora · Monado SLAM Datasets</span><h1 id=\"_top\">Monado: HP Reverb G2</h1><p class=sd-type>HP Reverb G2, tracking-camera pair + IMU @ 1 kHz</p></div><figure class=sd-plate><div class=sd-frame><img src=\"/media/examples/monado/hp-reverb-g2.jpg\" alt=\"HP Reverb G2 headset, front view\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\"></div><figcaption><a href=\"https://www.hp.com/us-en/newsroom/press-releases/2020/hp-valve-microsoft-next-gen-virtual-reality-headset.html\">Photo: HP, Reverb G2 press release ↗︎</a></figcaption></figure><div class=sd-cta><div class=sd-buttons><a class=\"sd-btn primary\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/collabora/monado-slam-datasets\">Downloads: Monado SLAM Datasets ↗︎</a><a class=\"sd-btn\" href=\"/benchmark/results/\">All recordings and tools: Results →</a><a class=\"sd-btn\" href=\"/sensors/hp-reverb-g2/\">HP Reverb G2 in the Sensor wiki →</a></div></div><div class=sd-specs><dl class=sd-rows><div class=sd-row><dt>Cameras</dt><dd>2 × 640×480 grayscale, 30 Hz (front pair)</dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>IMU</dt><dd>About 1 kHz</dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Board</dt><dd>AprilGrid 6×6, tag 30 mm</dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Format</dt><dd>EuRoC mav0</dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Licence</dt><dd>CC BY 4.0</dd></div></dl></div></div></div>", "glance": "<p>One MVIS camera + IMU run on the HP Reverb G2 recording imucalib01 (round 1), and how close it lands to the calibration Monado ships with the data.</p><div class=band><figure class=demo><video src=\"/media/hero/hero_mgc_960.mp4\" poster=\"/media/hero/hero_mgc_960.jpg\" autoplay muted loop playsinline controls preload=metadata></video><figcaption>The scene MVIS recovered from this dataset, as on the homepage. The values beside it come from this page&#x27;s run.</figcaption></figure><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=tiles><div><span>Reprojection median</span><b>0.13<small> px</small></b></div><div><span>cam0–cam1 baseline</span><b>108.5<small> mm</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 td</span><b>−1.23<small> ms</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 lever arm</span><b>53.9<small> mm</small></b></div></div></div></div><p class=sd-note>Reprojection is how far, in pixels, the detected corners lie from where the solve puts them. td is the camera–IMU time offset, and the lever arm is the camera–IMU position offset.</p>", "process": "<p>MVIS's own player, from this run: the detected board corners, then the rig's path as the solve refines it. Press <b>Play</b> or drag the bar; pick a camera card to look through that camera. We publish no camera images.</p><div class=proc-wrap><button type=button class=proc-open hidden><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 220\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><polygon points=\"253.6,98.0 312.5,119.8 307.5,43.7 248.6,21.9 253.6,98.0\" fill=\"var(--strong)\" fill-opacity=\".1\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\"/><polyline points=\"237.2,87.3 248.9,80.7 249.9,78.1 236.2,81.7 214.3,87.6 193.7,90.7 177.5,92.9 170.0,96.0 176.9,97.4 194.9,91.1 216.9,84.1 237.7,75.9 251.0,70.3 248.9,68.6 231.8,74.3 206.7,85.5 181.3,95.2 163.9,101.3 167.2,101.2 190.7,91.1 217.4,80.4 238.3,72.9 245.4,70.6 233.7,75.1 211.0,83.6 189.5,92.9 173.0,98.4 166.2,102.9 176.4,103.0 197.7,98.4 217.2,93.2 225.7,83.0 226.7,55.1 223.2,38.6 220.7,70.4 219.2,108.1 218.8,140.9 216.9,123.3 209.7,86.2 204.3,55.0 203.4,58.0 205.4,99.4 208.6,136.2 206.4,137.1 196.2,101.9 184.6,67.5 179.3,50.3 178.9,81.0 178.3,122.4 182.0,139.3 198.6,102.6 223.0,81.4 245.5,85.8 246.8,92.8 221.0,84.5 188.1,73.8 166.8,68.1 171.6,66.3 195.0,75.3 226.4,88.3 240.9,100.7 221.4,95.2 184.4,79.5 148.6,74.6 128.1,78.4 138.6,71.7 169.1,73.8 205.9,88.5 225.7,104.4 204.8,97.3 165.4,79.3 132.7,70.2 128.8,69.1 161.4,70.5 201.4,80.7 226.3,83.2 227.6,79.6 225.9,79.7 227.0,80.9 229.5,78.3 232.8,76.8 233.8,69.9 235.1,69.7 232.0,73.1 227.2,73.7 220.7,78.0 211.7,77.4 203.8,78.9 196.3,86.2 193.3,80.1 185.6,81.9 184.2,88.0 190.2,96.1 195.0,92.3 190.6,96.8 191.0,106.3 190.8,90.1 188.7,76.0 195.2,86.9 197.4,108.3 199.3,120.6 195.5,104.4 189.7,71.3 189.7,64.2 201.8,84.9 212.1,111.1 221.9,112.7 220.2,70.8 210.6,40.0 211.1,38.2 224.3,70.2 232.6,115.7 234.9,123.8 231.5,82.2 227.9,46.4 224.8,26.1 225.0,33.0 223.8,67.6 226.7,93.6 245.6,91.8 265.4,90.9 257.5,87.0 233.3,75.6 207.8,71.4 202.5,71.7 218.0,73.0 236.2,82.1 255.2,90.7 259.8,89.5 246.3,76.0 224.6,70.1 201.9,74.0 205.9,76.9 228.6,78.6 253.0,86.5 240.3,79.6 219.9,74.6 214.3,78.5 210.6,78.8 197.9,54.8 193.1,30.3 208.0,44.5 231.7,82.4 251.3,102.8 260.0,86.4 257.4,62.3 238.2,46.6 214.5,38.5 198.6,36.8 191.3,31.4 199.0,20.0 205.4,30.0 209.9,43.9 220.3,56.5 224.9,60.6 233.3,57.9 236.1,69.4 234.5,64.8 240.9,65.9 254.7,77.0 255.8,82.3 247.6,99.1 225.9,106.7 227.1,94.2 221.3,78.1 214.4,58.9 192.4,40.7 178.6,20.2 208.9,45.8 222.7,65.0 220.8,83.9 219.5,96.4 225.1,76.6 229.6,44.5 227.9,25.9 211.8,29.7 201.2,33.5 213.4,52.4 221.2,55.3 228.5,47.8 226.4,34.2 221.0,34.0 225.1,55.8 224.4,79.7 206.9,75.2 200.6,49.7 198.2,26.6 201.9,41.1 222.2,65.8 241.7,64.6 253.1,58.7 254.9,52.5 231.3,49.1 220.3,32.3 215.7,30.9 171.8,37.3 123.6,52.8 87.5,89.9 111.6,198.1 114.2,200.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg><span>Explore in 3D (about 2 MB)</span></button><div class=\"mvv\" data-mvv=\"scene\" data-mode=\"site\" data-src=\"/media/examples/monado/views0.json\"></div></div>", "result": "<p>The solved positions and orientations, to scale in the IMU frame. Drag sideways to orbit. Tap a sensor to see its values.</p><div class=map><div class=stage><canvas id=rig tabindex=0 aria-label=\"3D map of the cameras and IMU\"></canvas><div class=tools><button data-view=iso type=button>3D</button><button data-view=front type=button>Front</button><button data-view=top type=button>Top</button><button data-view=side type=button>Side</button><button data-z=1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom in\">+</button><button data-z=-1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom out\">−</button></div></div><div class=panel><div class=picks id=picks></div><div id=info></div></div></div><div class=scroll><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Sensor</th><th>fx, fy, cx, cy px</th><th>Lever mm</th><th>log(R) rad</th><th>td ms</th><th>t_ga ms</th><th>Reprojection px</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>cam0</th><td>269.9, 270.2, 322.5, 229.2</td><td>[−52.0, +13.3, +5.2]</td><td>[−0.3458, +0.0753, +1.5383]</td><td>−1.23</td><td></td><td>0.121</td></tr><tr><th>cam1</th><td>268.9, 268.8, 323.8, 237.0</td><td>[+56.5, +14.1, +5.4]</td><td>[−0.0749, +0.3457, +1.5942]</td><td>−1.22</td><td></td><td>0.138</td></tr><tr><th>IMU (base)</th><td></td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>+2.51 ± 0.21</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=note>Lever arms and rotations are each sensor in the base IMU frame; rotation is log(R) in rad. td is the time offset to the base IMU, t_imu = t_sensor + td. Reprojection is the median per camera (all cameras: median 0.130 px): how well the model fits the corners, not how accurate it is.</p>", "check": "<p>Reference: <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/collabora/monado-slam-datasets\">The Basalt calibration Monado ships with the HP Reverb G2 data (MG_reverb_g2, extras, calibration)</a>.</p><div class=scroll><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>MVIS</th><th>Monado (Basalt)</th><th>Difference</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=grp><th colspan=4>cam0</th></tr><tr><td>Lever mm</td><td>[−51.96, +13.34, +5.19]</td><td>[−51.95, +12.66, +5.70]</td><td>Δp 0.85 mm</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[−0.3458, +0.0753, +1.5383]</td><td>[−0.3456, +0.0756, +1.5383]</td><td>Δθ 0.34 mrad</td></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>269.92</td><td>not comparable: Basalt used an 8-parameter radial-tangential lens</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>−1.226</td><td>fixed at 0 in that file, not an estimate</td><td></td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=4>cam1</th></tr><tr><td>Lever mm</td><td>[+56.53, +14.08, +5.38]</td><td>[+56.45, +13.37, +5.82]</td><td>Δp 0.84 mm</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[−0.0749, +0.3457, +1.5942]</td><td>[−0.0726, +0.3445, +1.5945]</td><td>Δθ 2.34 mrad</td></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>268.88</td><td>not comparable: Basalt used an 8-parameter radial-tangential lens</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>−1.218</td><td>fixed at 0 in that file, not an estimate</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=note>Δp is the distance between the two lever arms. Δθ = ‖log(R<sub>a</sub><sup>T</sup> R<sub>b</sub>)‖, the angle between the two rotations. A reference, not ground truth: it was solved by another tool on the same kind of data.</p><p class=note>Monado ships a second, equidistant calibration of the same headset. Its rotations differ from this file&#x27;s by about 4.5 mrad, so a few mrad is within how much the references themselves disagree.</p>", "config": "<p>The marked lines are the choices that matter for this rig:</p><ul class=list><li><code>board.tag_size</code>: The 30 mm tag. A wrong tag size gives a calibration that converges cleanly and is uniformly wrong in scale.</li><li><code>input.window_mode</code>: MVIS picks the 80 s window with the most motion.</li><li><code>camera_input.cameras</code>: cam1 is added to the graph at 8 Hz, which keeps the solve small.</li><li><code>solve.estimate_t_ga</code>: Estimates t_ga, the time offset between the gyroscope and the accelerometer.</li><li><code>estimate.camera.intrinsics</code>: Camera intrinsics stay free in the camera + IMU solve.</li></ul><p class=note>This is the config of the run on this page, with every path cut to its file name. Point the paths at your copy.</p><p>The solve took about 3 min on one desktop. It writes <code>cam_imu.json</code>, a calibration YAML and a report beside the config.</p><dl class=ex-kv><dt>MVIS</dt><dd>MVIS main, example solves of 2026-11-10</dd><dt>Run date</dt><dd>2026-11-10</dd><dt>Data</dt><dd><a href=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/collabora/monado-slam-datasets\">Monado SLAM Datasets →</a></dd><dt>Config</dt><dd><code>monado_mgc_imucalib01_cam_imu.yaml</code>, above</dd><dt>Command</dt><dd><code>mvis cam-imu -c monado_mgc_imucalib01_cam_imu.yaml</code></dd></dl>", "dataset": "<div class=two><div><ul class=list><li>Recording MGC imucalib01, round 1, from the Monado SLAM Datasets (Collabora). It shows the board to the front camera pair, cam0 and cam1.</li><li>Cameras: 640 × 480 grayscale at 30 Hz, fitted with the equidistant lens model, as in the MVIS regression config for this headset. IMU at about 1 kHz.</li><li>Board: AprilGrid 6×6, tag 30 mm, spacing 0.3, t36h11. The tag is much smaller than the usual 88 mm, and board size scales every translation.</li><li>Solve window: 41.6 s.</li></ul><p>Download: <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/collabora/monado-slam-datasets\">Monado SLAM Datasets →</a> The recordings are listed there, not copied here.</p></div><div><figure class=board><svg viewBox=\"-18.0 -18.0 261.0 261.0\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"AprilGrid 6 by 6, to scale\"><rect x=\"-18.0\" y=\"-18.0\" width=\"261.0\" height=\"261.0\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path fill=\"#111\" d=\"M-9.00 -9.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM30.00 -9.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM69.00 -9.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM108.00 -9.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM147.00 -9.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM186.00 -9.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM225.00 -9.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM-9.00 30.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM30.00 30.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM69.00 30.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM108.00 30.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM147.00 30.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM186.00 30.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM225.00 30.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM-9.00 69.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM30.00 69.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM69.00 69.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM108.00 69.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM147.00 69.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM186.00 69.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM225.00 69.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM-9.00 108.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM30.00 108.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM69.00 108.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM108.00 108.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM147.00 108.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM186.00 108.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM225.00 108.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM-9.00 147.00h9.00v9.00h-9.00zM30.